From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, shlwapi: ExplorerBrowser view state, SHGetViewStatePropertyBag (3705)

shell32, shlwapi: ExplorerBrowser view state, SHGetViewStatePropertyBag

SHGetViewStatePropertyBag now returns a property bag kept in the registry
(per folder, for all folders, inherit bags, user or machine, with the
defaults search unless it is switched off). The registry property bag also
reads and writes byte arrays. IExplorerBrowser::SetPropertyBag names the bag
in which the browser keeps the view mode and flags of each folder (written
when a navigation begins and when the browser is destroyed, read when a
folder's view is made), SetEmptyText sets the text of an empty view,
IShellBrowser::GetViewStateStream hands out a stream kept in that bag,
TranslateAcceleratorSB handles Backspace and Alt+Left/Right, the connection
point container and connection point enumerators work, and OnStateChange
without a site succeeds.
